From bad0454169d5417016c4b872cc583fa31e121048 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:22:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: GPU-bound frame start pacing; GPU timers in 1 frame in
 8; draw timing off by default

When 48 of the last 64 frames got their spare time from a busy GPU, the
hold-back aims at the 7th smallest spare time of those frames, a late
frame takes off what it came late by plus 1 ms (instead of halving),
adds 1 ms margin (instead of 3), and growth resumes after 15 frames at up
to 0.5 ms per frame. Cap-bound pacing is unchanged.

The pass meter puts its timestamps into the command lists of 1 frame in
8 with VKD3D_FEX_PASSES=1 (2 = every frame). Draw timing needs
VKD3D_FEX_DRAWS=1. The present report adds the GPU time per frame of
frames with and without pass timers.
